WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.185
Lesson 2.3.

00:00:02.185 --> 00:00:03.750
Providing liquidity.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:06.012
By the end of this lesson, you'll

00:00:06.012 --> 00:00:08.473
be able to estimate an LP position's

00:00:08.473 --> 00:00:10.535
fee income from real pool data.

00:00:11.835 --> 00:00:13.125
Here's the plan.

00:00:13.125 --> 00:00:14.810
First, the key ideas.

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:17.525
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:17.525 --> 00:00:19.050
Then, your checklist.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.212
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:22.512 --> 00:00:25.354
When you LP you deposit both tokens and

00:00:25.354 --> 00:00:28.053
receive a share of the pool (a token,

00:00:28.053 --> 00:00:31.053
or an NFT for concentrated positions).

00:00:31.053 --> 00:00:32.968
You earn your share of swap fees.

00:00:32.968 --> 00:00:36.050
In return, your token mix changes as traders move

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:39.678
the price: you become the counterparty to every trade.

00:00:39.678 --> 00:00:44.038
Fee APR estimate: fee APR ≈ (daily volume ×

00:00:44.038 --> 00:00:47.605
fee tier × your pool share × 365) ÷

00:00:47.605 --> 00:00:52.362
your deposit For a full-range pool your share =

00:00:52.362 --> 00:00:57.118
deposit ÷ pool TVL, so this simplifies to daily

00:00:57.118 --> 00:01:00.587
volume × fee tier × 365 ÷ TVL. Use

00:01:00.587 --> 00:01:04.553
a 30-day average volume, not today's.

00:01:04.553 --> 00:01:07.316
Volume spikes on volatile days, which are also

00:01:07.316 --> 00:01:09.903
the days you take the most impermanent loss.

00:01:11.203 --> 00:01:13.718
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:01:13.718 --> 00:01:19.409
Pool T.V.L. $10M, 30-day average daily volume $2M, fee

00:01:19.409 --> 00:01:25.090
tier 0.3%: If volume halves, your fee A.P.R. halves.

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:26.765
If a lot more T.V.L. joins

00:01:26.765 --> 00:01:28.865
the pool, your share shrinks.

00:01:28.865 --> 00:01:35.450
Daily pool fees equals 2,000,000 times 0.003 = $6,000.

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:39.280
Your $10,000 equals 0.1% share to $6

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:42.593
a day to about 21.9% fee A.P.R.

00:01:42.593 --> 00:01:46.112
(before impermanent loss and gas).

00:01:47.412 --> 00:01:48.872
Here's your checklist.

00:01:48.872 --> 00:01:50.407
Do it now, for real.

00:01:50.407 --> 00:01:54.292
First, Fee APR calculated from 30-day volume.

00:01:54.292 --> 00:01:58.082
Next, I'm OK holding 100% of either token.

00:01:58.082 --> 00:02:02.197
Then, Entry prices recorded for the "vs hold" benchmark.

00:02:02.197 --> 00:02:05.590
And finally, Exit rule written (volume drops,

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:08.320
trend starts, fees stop covering IL).

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:10.830
Question 1.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:17.580
Pool TVL $5M, daily volume $1M, 0.05% fee.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:19.395
Full-range fee APR?

00:02:23.815 --> 00:02:29.958
The answer: 1,000,000 × 0.0005 ×

00:02:29.958 --> 00:02:34.425
365 ÷ 5,000,000 = 3.65%.

00:02:35.725 --> 00:02:36.970
Question 2.

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:38.515
Why use 30-day volume?

00:02:42.935 --> 00:02:46.118
The answer: Single-day spikes overstate fee income,

00:02:46.118 --> 00:02:48.077
and they happen on the days you

00:02:48.077 --> 00:02:49.975
take the most impermanent loss.

00:02:51.275 --> 00:02:52.545
Question 3.

00:02:52.545 --> 00:02:55.270
What happens to your share if TVL doubles?

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:01.636
The answer: It halves, and so do

00:03:01.636 --> 00:03:03.405
your fees, at the same volume.

00:03:04.705 --> 00:03:07.220
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:10.352
Next up, Lesson 2.4: Impermanent

00:03:10.352 --> 00:03:12.155
loss & true LP P&L.
